  "implementation": [
    "Configurable host, transfer protocol, HCA, bootstrap port and reference paths in the PD runtime fixture retain loopback/TCP defaults.",
    "Separate foreground P supervisor runs target-only P with overlap/radix reuse, exports a readiness descriptor, checks its child and reaps the serving tree on SIGTERM.",
    "Cross-node driver validates descriptor identity, reaches the external P over HTTP and runs D locally with RDMA. Observation failures raise instead of claiming the peer is terminal.",
    "Shared RDMACaptureRuntimeBase retains complete existing data assertions, stops each owned D, and validates fresh-process readback. Optional manifest-reference output enables final readback after external P exits.",
    "No production wire or Mooncake Master API change was necessary."
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "Selected KV values and raw top-128 logits/vocab IDs exactly match independent observations of the actual online P/D source; full-vocabulary LSE uses rtol=atol=1e-6.",
    "Tokens, response/loss masks, positions, KV validity and final accepted/terminal boundaries match generated responses.",
    "Chunked and cached prefixes, single-token replies, actual two-request D batches and accepted/rejected verify paths are included.",
    "Speculative D source frames are verify frames; no target prefill is added for data capture. The target-KV draft projects the received prefix and incrementally incorporates accepted rows.",
    "Four cases publish 22 main samples plus one synthetic-draft seed. Twelve selected missing/stale-handoff or cancelled requests fail capture without publishing partial samples.",
    "After every D exits, a fresh process reads all published samples. After the whole file, the external P supervisor and its serving tree exit before another complete readback.",
    "Shared files carry only configuration, source-reference observations and manifest refs; serving KV and Store tensor payloads use Mooncake."
  ],
